   "gap": "Owned by w02b-p15-032: not every evidence or proof claim in printed pp.305-316 is accounted for. Unaccounted: (a) p.313, lower probabilities from an arbitrary credal set satisfy P_*(A u B) >= P_*(A)+P_*(B) only for disjoint A,B, whereas belief functions are superadditive at every order. This contrast is neither proved nor bounded (the handbook proves only the belief-function side, thm:p15-r47-focal). (b) p.313, robust dominance satisfies the sure-thing principle and maxmin resolves Ellsberg: these claims are not accounted for. (c) p.312, every convex set of probabilities is representable by lower previsions on some family of gambles: only an indirect closure qualification is given at rationality-4-7.tex:461-464, with no explicit statement of the closedness condition or the bounding of the claim.",
